<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/insights/">← Back to insights</a><div class="section-label">Strategy</div><h1>Zero-Based Budgeting for MSMEs: A Step-by-Step Guide to Rebuilding Your Cost Structure</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body"><p>Zero-Based Budgeting (ZBB) is one of the most powerful cost management tools available to MSME leaders — and one of the most misunderstood. Here is how to apply it correctly.</p><h4>What ZBB Is (and Is Not)</h4><p>ZBB is not about cutting costs arbitrarily. It is about requiring every line of expenditure to justify its existence from zero — rather than simply incrementing last year's budget by a percentage. In practice, this means asking: "If we were building this budget from scratch today, would we spend money on this?" not "How much more than last year do we need?"</p><h4>The 4-Step Process</h4><p>Step 1: Map every cost to a business activity. Step 2: For each activity, ask: does this directly drive revenue, reduce risk, or fulfil a legal requirement? Step 3: For activities that do not pass this test, eliminate, reduce, or outsource. Step 4: For activities that pass, benchmark the cost against market alternatives and renegotiate where overpaying.</p><h4>What We Typically Find</h4><p>In every ZBB exercise we have conducted for MSME clients, we find 15–25% of overhead spend that either has no clear business justification, or is significantly above market rate. That is pure margin improvement.</p></div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
